---
# Checklist:
# - [x] Minimal Resources
# - [x] Minimal storage -> 10Gi, the default: a development instance renders a handful of
#       schemas and caches a few downloads
# - [x] 1 Replica -> one node, one volume

resources:
  requests:
    cpu: 100m
    # T-4473: dev, kubectl top 2026-10-17 21:22-22:22Z: median 96, peak 105Mi. T-5897: dev working set 2026-10-25..28 (Prometheus, 3 days, supervisor):
    # 694Mi since the WAL archive grew (T-5772), + 20 %: the request says what it holds.
    # T-5926 (dev 2026-10-29, Prometheus): 24 h max 729Mi (the 10-28 WAL purge); at 10:00Z working
    # set 624Mi of which RSS 395Mi, the rest page cache of written objects the kernel reclaims at
    # the limit. RSS follows the object count (~8,700 WAL segments a day, retention 2d) and RustFS
    # 1.0.4 offers no setting that bounds it: RUSTFS_OBJECT_DATA_CACHE_ENABLE=false, allocator
    # reclaim, reclaim-on-write and direct-IO writes changed nothing in a local A/B. A burst of
    # 80 x 16 MiB WAL + a 256 MiB base peaks at 380-445Mi and falls back to ~180Mi in 3 min.
    # Fewer objects (less WAL, T-5772) is what lowers it.
    memory: 832Mi
  limits:
    cpu: 1000m
    memory: 1024Mi
